    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "34e5aa3b-db10-40a1-893d-79e98cd3f2f4",
      "key": "fc50e27d-8a4b-4b73-a058-e8dd96153224",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Features"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E4* hotel\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHalf board accommodation\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAll excursion travel \u0026amp; guided tours included\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EEntrance fees to non-National Trust properties included\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBoat excursion on Day 3 included\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EExecutive coach throughout\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBlue Badge guide included on Days 2 to 4\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EGratuities included\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "1d09b5af-b95a-4af5-b8f2-323db029e817",
      "key": "018536fa-f747-4a28-8a91-d638464a2c99",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Accommodation"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EWe stay four nights at the 4* Park Royal Hotel (\u003Ca href=\u0022https://www.theparkroyal.co.uk\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noopener\u0022\u003Ewww.theparkroyal.co.uk\u003C/a\u003E) in Stretton. Facilities at the hotel include a restaurant, bar, swimming pool, gymnasium, Jacuzzi, and sauna, and all rooms are en suite and feature television, telephone, hairdryer, and tea \u0026amp; coffee making facilities. A set 3 course dinner will be served on the first evening, and a choice 3 course dinner will be served on the remaining three nights.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a00f052f-2581-4b24-a04e-a49db5a87615",
      "key": "e8f751d8-dcf9-4d6f-a37b-9b07eb86ae59",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Organiser"
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureDescription",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "For more information on this tour contact your Group Organiser"
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureSummary",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EOnce you have received your Confirmation and Invoice, you can pay your final balance.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "2d9b0603-29ef-423a-8d3e-d9c039d3d7b1",
      "key": "174699fd-11c8-4f67-9b4e-43f18fa2ee5f",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Sights"
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureDescription",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": ""
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ELittle Moreton Hall\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EManchester Art Gallery \u2013 guided tour\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EQuarry Bank Mill \u0026amp; Styal Estate\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAnderton Boat Lift Visitor Centre \u0026amp; cruise\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EErddig\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe Lowry \u2013 guided tour\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ELyme Park\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ERHS Garden Bridgewater \u2013 guided tour\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureSummary",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "c4b3a613-0d2c-4470-8d06-f7efea52d6e0",
      "key": "9ad52a60-fb61-4d44-a2b0-69590653f31b",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "In this page"
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyNavigationInPageItems",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": [
            "e5ce4717-67c8-4f31-982d-3185140539f5",
            "fc50e27d-8a4b-4b73-a058-e8dd96153224",
            "018536fa-f747-4a28-8a91-d638464a2c99",
            "174699fd-11c8-4f67-9b4e-43f18fa2ee5f",
            "940e3628-87ef-42ba-a433-1daf170042c0",
            "3b5a42a3-3468-4002-8601-53c2cce32661",
            "e8f751d8-dcf9-4d6f-a37b-9b07eb86ae59"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "837beecf-4239-4b3d-b683-1d611af3da2e",
      "key": "e5ce4717-67c8-4f31-982d-3185140539f5",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Itinerary"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Ch3\u003EDay 1\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EWe depart by private executive coach from our designated pick up points. En route to our hotel we visit the National Trust\u2019s Little Moreton Hall in Cheshire. Begun in 1504 and completed 100 years later, Little Moreton Hall is regarded as the finest example of a timber-framed moated house in the country. We then check in at the 4* Park Royal Hotel at Stretton for a four night stay on a half board basis.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 2\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EOur Blue Badge guide meets us at our hotel this morning and accompanies us throughout the day. A guided tour at the Manchester Art Gallery this morning introduces us to one of the country\u2019s finest art collections including pre-Raphaelite paintings, craft and design, and early 20th century British art, all set in spectacular Victorian and contemporary surroundings. The National Trust\u2019s Quarry Bank Mill and Styal Estate near Wilmslow is our destination this afternoon. This restored Georgian cotton mill tells the story of \u2018King Cotton\u2019 from a bale of raw cotton to finished cloth, and the original Apprentice House recreates the 1830s atmosphere of the lives of child workers.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 3\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EWe firstly visit the Anderton Boat Lift Visitor Centre. The Boat Lift was built by Edwin Clark in 1875 to lift cargo boats the 50 feet from the River Weaver to the Trent \u0026amp; Mersey Canal. Whilst at the Visitor Centre, we enjoy a memorable boat excursion which travels along the River Weaver and through the Anderton Boat Lift. We continue with our Blue Badge guide to the National Trust\u2019s Erddig property, one of the most fascinating houses in Britain with an evocative range of outbuildings and state rooms displaying most of their original 18th and 19th century furnishings.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 4\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EWith our Blue Badge guide this morning we enjoy a guided tour of The Lowry. Set in a magnificent waterside location at the heart of the redeveloped Salford Quays, The Lowry houses the biggest public collection of works by LS Lowry with around 350 paintings and drawings, ranging across Lowry\u0026#39;s artistic career. This afternoon we visit the National Trust\u2019s Lyme Park property. Originally a Tudor house, Lyme was transformed by the Venetian architect Leoni into an Italianate palace, lavishly decorated with Mortlake tapestries and Grinling Gibbons wood carvings.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 5\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EAfter checking out of our hotel and en route home we enjoy a guided tour at RHS Garden Bridgewater, so named after the nearby canal. A stunning new 156-acre garden, RHS Garden Bridgewater is being created in the heart of the North West by bringing back to life the lost historic grounds at Worsley New Hall in Salford. This is one of the largest gardening projects in Europe, designed mainly by Tom Stuart Smith. In 2019 at the Chelsea show, his garden highlighted the main features for Bridgewater\u2019s future. The RHS tells us \u201CBridgewater includes one of the largest walled gardens in the UK\u201D. There are many areas to discover here, kitchen, paradise and Chinese gardens, restored Victorian greenhouses and much more. Worsley New Hall was built for the Earl of Ellesmere in the 1840\u2019s, survived a fire and was once visited by Queen Victoria and King Edward VII. It served as a Red Cross hospital during WW1 and was a training ground of the Lancashire Fusiliers in WW2. Eventually this grand Gothic style mansion, designed by Edward Blore, was demolished in the 1940\u2019s, with its gardens gradually disappearing. Then along came the RHS. Taking carefully selected comfort stops en route, we return back to our original pick up points.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureDescription",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": ""
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureSummary",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ENB:- Please note we reserve the right to alter the above itinerary if required for operational\nreasons. Given the historic nature of the places visited, a certain degree of walking will be involved, and this holiday may not be suitable for those with mobility concerns.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
